			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add Disable=true master kill-switch for bisecting regressions\n\nIntroduce a build-time and runtime gate that strips all Land customizations so the workbench loads as close to upstream VS Code on Tauri as possible:\n\n1. **Disable=true gate** (`import.meta.env.Disable`): When set, SkyBridge short-circuits without registering any of the ~100 `sky://*` Tauri event listeners. The layout script skips Bootstrap (Wind's Effect-TS layer), TelemetryBridge, and InstallSkyBridge entirely. The smoke test harness is replaced with AutoDiagnoseInput.\n\n2. **AutoDiagnoseInput diagnostic**: New hands-off probe that runs only under Disable=true. Reports to console which editor instance has focus, classifies it (chat input / file editor / search / settings), and tells the user whether typing SHOULD work. The most common \"typing doesn't work\" issue is the user typing into VS Code's chat panel which silently drops keystrokes when Cocoon is unavailable.\n\n3. **Remove eager focus restore**: The previous phaseChanged handler that forced focus to Monaco on every phase >= 3 caused regressions - it fired twice (phase 3 and phase 4 ~15s later), yanking focus away from search boxes after the user typed one character. Mountain's MainWindow.show() + set_focus() already lands first-responder correctly at phase 3, so the redundant Sky-side re-focus is dropped.\n\n4. **Flag naming**: Rename `LAND_SMOKE_TEST` / `land-smoke` to `Smoke` (PascalCase, matching Land's env-var convention in `.env.Land.Diagnostics`).\n\nUseful for bisecting whether a regression lives in our customizations (still broken under Disable) or upstream/Tauri/WKWebView (still broken even with Disable=true).",
			"SHA": "e5259308f3d0ea7101cf657928984c778d418286"
		},
